格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"deepseek harness对话和代码状态回退插件 | DSH — rewind conversation and workspace state, powered by a persistent Change Ledger","id":"gh:1333100390","install_available":true,"language":"JavaScript","name":"dsh-turn-rewind","slug":"Anionex/dsh-turn-rewind","topics":["agent-rewind","cordis-plugin","deepseek-harness","dsh","dsh-plugin","marisa-plugin","restore-point","turn-rewind","workspace-safety"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"deepseek harness对话和代码状态回退插件 | DSH — rewind conversation and workspace state, powered by a persistent"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"ss对话和代码状态回退插件 | DSH — rewind conversation and workspace state, powered by a persistent Change Ledger"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# DSH Turn Rewind"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"中文说明"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"Message-anchored project-file recovery for DeepSeek Harness, with an option to restart from the rest"},{"id":"p4s2","text":"red project-file recovery for DeepSeek Harness, with an option to restart from the restored request."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"**Turn Rewind** is the user-facing feature, repository, and Profile Bundle name. **Change Ledger** i"},{"id":"p5s2","text":"s the durable restore engine underneath it: the `ctx.changeLedger` service, on-disk format, and stor"},{"id":"p5s3","text":"age path keep that name because they describe the reusable snapshot and recovery layer rather than t"},{"id":"p5s4","text":"he Web action alone."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"Change Ledger gives a DSH session an explicit safety boundary around workspace mutations:"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"It never commits, stashes, resets, switches branches, edits the Git index, or decides automatically "},{"id":"p8s2","text":"that a change should be reverted."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"## What's new"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"Most recent work first:"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"- **File rewind works in ordinary directories (0.3.0)** — when the working directory is not a Git re"},{"id":"p11s2","text":"pository it is snapshotted as an ordinary directory (`.git` and `node_modules` excluded by default, "},{"id":"p11s3","text":"plus an optional `.dsh-rewindignore`), so messages-only rewind is no longer the only option.\n- **The"},{"id":"p11s4","text":" fastest path is now the default (0.3.8)** — the new `auto` mode uses Git-native checkpoints in a Gi"},{"id":"p11s5","text":"t worktree (reusing the repository object database, so committed content is never stored twice) and "},{"id":"p11s6","text":"the plugin's own store for ordinary directories.\n- **Unchanged files are no longer re-read (0.3.5)**"},{"id":"p11s7","text":" — each workspace keeps a persistent path identity cache; a measured 20 000-file / 351 MB workspace "},{"id":"p11s8","text":"dropped from 237 s to about 7 s per capture.\n- **One oversized file no longer discards a whole check"},{"id":"p11s9","text":"point (0.3.3)** — it is skipped and reported while the rest is still captured, and a restore never t"},{"id":"p11s10","text":"ouches a path its checkpoint did not record, so a file that was too large then and small now is neve"},{"id":"p11s11","text":"r deleted.\n- **Checkpoint budget 5 s → 60 s, parallel capture (0.3.4)** — a 5-second budget in a lar"},{"id":"p11s12","text":"ge directory could only ever report a skip.\n- **Rewind button and messages-only fixes (0.2.2 / 0.2.3"},{"id":"p11s13","text":")** — adapted to the DSH 0.1.2-alpha client hooks and restored the messages-only mode that the Host "},{"id":"p11s14","text":"rejected.\n- **Settings card matches the official cards (0.3.6 / 0.3.7)** — one collapsed row that ex"},{"id":"p11s15","text":"pands, consistent with every other plugin card."},{"id":"p12s1","text":"## Preview"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"Rewind appears as an icon-only third action under each user message, after its timestamp and native "},{"id":"p13s2","text":"rs as an icon-only third action under each user message, after its timestamp and native Copy action:"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"Opening it shows the affected files and offers three choices: restore the files and restart from bef"},{"id":"p14s2","text":"ore that message, restore only the files, or rewind only the messages and leave the files untouched:"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"## Why it has a Change Ledger engine"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"A diff button can show current changes, but it does not own a durable restore lifecycle. Change Ledg"},{"id":"p16s2","text":"utton can show current changes, but it does not own a durable restore lifecycle. Change Ledger owns:"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"- content-addressed restore-point manifests;\n- Git worktree, HEAD, branch, and in-progress-operation"},{"id":"p17s2","text":" fences;\n- stale-plan detection between review and mutation;\n- exact two-step confirmation plus DSH "},{"id":"p17s3","text":"human approval;\n- automatic pre-restore rescue points;\n- post-restore hash verification;\n- rollback "},{"id":"p17s4","text":"after a failed restore;\n- startup reconciliation of interrupted restore journals;\n- a public `ctx.ch"},{"id":"p17s5","text":"angeLedger` service that other plugins can consume."},{"id":"p18s1","text":"The durable format is documented in docs/FORMAT.md. The security and failure model is documented in "},{"id":"p18s2","text":"format is documented in docs/FORMAT.md. The security and failure model is documented in SECURITY.md."},{"id":"p19s1","text":"## Safety contract"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"- **Explicit only:** nothing is restored automatically — every restore starts from the user pressing"},{"id":"p20s2","text":" the final button in the Web dialog, or from an explicit call through the service API.\n- **Read befo"},{"id":"p20s3","text":"re write:** the dialog preview generates an expiring, session-bound plan from the current tree and c"},{"id":"p20s4","text":"hanges no files.\n- **Human gate:** the dialog's reviewed impact plus the final restore button is the"},{"id":"p20s5","text":" human decision; direct mutation requests without a live session-bound plan pair fail closed.\n- **Re"},{"id":"p20s6","text":"scue before mutation:** every restore captures the current eligible tree as a durable rescue point b"},{"id":"p20s7","text":"efore changing a path.\n- **No silent omission:** unsupported submodules, sparse checkouts, oversized"},{"id":"p20s8","text":" files, aggregate limits, and unsupported file types fail point creation.\n- **No path escape:** ever"},{"id":"p20s9","text":"y durable path is canonical and workspace-relative; restore refuses symlink parents and non-empty di"},{"id":"p20s10","text":"rectory replacement.\n- **No stale overwrite:** selected paths and the reviewed HEAD/branch/operation"},{"id":"p20s11","text":" fence are checked again at apply time. Any relevant post-review change invalidates the plan.\n- **No"},{"id":"p20s12","text":" Git control-plane mutation:** the index, branch, HEAD, stash, and commits remain untouched."},{"id":"p21s1","text":"## Scope"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"Two workspace kinds are supported and selected from the Session's own directory:"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"**Normal Git worktree**"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"- tracked files, including currently missing tracked paths;\n- untracked files not excluded by `.giti"},{"id":"p24s2","text":"gnore` or other standard Git excludes;\n- regular files, binary or text;\n- symbolic links;\n- executab"},{"id":"p24s3","text":"le and other portable permission bits."},{"id":"p25s1","text":"**Ordinary directory (the Session directory is not a Git repository)**"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"- every regular file and symbolic link below it; links are captured as links and never followed;\n- `"},{"id":"p26s2","text":".git` and `node_modules` are excluded by default;\n- an optional `.dsh-rewindignore` in the directory"},{"id":"p26s3","text":" root adds `.gitignore`-style rules; the built-in exclusions are applied last and cannot be re-inclu"},{"id":"p26s4","text":"ded;\n- snapshot content is stored in the plugin's own content-addressed storage instead of the Git o"},{"id":"p26s5","text":"bject database;\n- running `git init` inside the directory changes the workspace mode, so earlier res"},{"id":"p26s6","text":"tore points stop applying (`WORKSPACE_MODE_CHANGED`) and a new message must create a new one."},{"id":"p27s1","text":"The following are rejected or deliberately outside the snapshot:"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"- sparse checkouts;\n- submodule gitlinks (create a restore point inside each submodule instead);\n- i"},{"id":"p28s2","text":"gnored files and files excluded by `.dsh-rewindignore`;\n- special files, sockets, devices, and named"},{"id":"p28s3","text":" pipes;\n- extended attributes, ACLs, ownership, timestamps, and hard-link topology;\n- the Git index "},{"id":"p28s4","text":"and repository metadata."},{"id":"p29s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}

